& [ObservedFault]
  + a package-wide native debug test was started after focused debug release Clippy and format gates had passed
  + the command was expected to reuse the existing cache but rebuilt enough targets to consume 5613961216 additional C-drive bytes
  + C-drive free space fell from 16370294784 bytes to 10756333568 bytes
  + twenty-two package targets reported failure: most evidence tests correctly saw the intentionally unrefreshed crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/lib.rs identity, several fresh executables met the governed Windows Application Control error 4551, and one pre-existing persistence test process met stack overflow
  + the new preparation integration target itself still passed eleven tests with zero failures

& [Cause]
  + the package gate was broader than the storage-restraint boundary and the cache-reuse assumption was not proven before launch
  + transitive evidence manifests had not yet been refreshed, so running their tests before rehash could not produce an exact-current-tree pass

& [Containment]
  + stop broad debug and release builds for the remainder of this checkpoint
  + do not delete compact relocate or clean native Cargo WSL or VHD storage without separate operator authorization
  + use only the already-built focused preparation surface bounded manifest rehash and read-only attribution checks
  + preserve error 4551 as host-policy refusal and do not bypass Windows Application Control
  + preserve D-drive WSL provider foreign work reserved root and reserved ref exclusions

& [Consequence]
  + no physical preparation Git worktree provider model MCP network D-drive WSL cleanup or foreign-work effect occurred
  + package-wide pass is unclaimed
  + exact implementation closure now requires transitive rehash focused replay and explicit disclosure of the storage overrun and broader-gate limitations

& [Prevention]
  + measure free space and prove the requested target set is already cached before any future expansion beyond a signed focused gate
  + refresh deterministic evidence identities before running evidence-bearing aggregate tests
  + treat a prior broad cache as unavailable after source changes unless current compiler artifacts prove otherwise
